         * Set to `RelayOnly` in container deployments without Secure Enclave /
         * TPM.
         */signingCapability: SigningCapability?, 
        /**
         * Set by the daemon's dispatch layer when the on-chain spending
         * policy has already determined this owner-level write must be
         * authorized on the phone. It exists for *self-managed* commands
         * (today `transfer`, `mpp_request` and `x402_request`), which bypass
         * the main policy gate
         * because they resolve a recipient inside their own `execute`
         * before an escalation intent can be built: the gate makes the
         * silent-vs-escalate decision and sets this flag, and the command
         * then yields an `AwaitingAuthorization` intent instead of signing
         * silently with the module key (which an over-cap amount would do,
         * only to revert at the on-chain guard). Always `false` for
         * commands that go through the normal gate -- there the gate
         * short-circuits before the command runs.
