     * `onetime`). `None` until registered on-chain.
     */
    public var period: Period?
    /**
     * Unix seconds of the allowance's last period reset. `None` until
     * registered on-chain.
     */
    public var lastReset: Int64?
    /**
     * Current pocket token balance (smallest units). `0` when the pocket ATA
     * does not exist yet.
     */
    public var balance: UInt64
    /**
     * Whether an on-chain `Agent` allowance account exists for this pocket.
     */
    public var registeredOnChain: Bool

    // Default memberwise initializers are never public by default, so we
    // declare one manually.
    public init(
        /**
         * CAIP-2 network id (`"solana:<genesis>"`).
         */network: String, 
        /**
         * SPL mint (base58) the pocket holds.
         */mint: String, 
        /**
         * The pocket token account (base58) -- the agent key's ATA for the mint.
         */pocketAddress: String, 
        /**
         * The agent's Ed25519 public key (base58); owns the pocket + signs
         * payments.
         */agentPubkey: String, 
        /**
         * The daemon's hardware P256 silent-signer key, SEC1-compressed (33 bytes)
         * as lowercase hex. This is the value the owner must bind as the agent's
         * `silent_key` when enrolling this pocket (`add_agent` on the mobile
         * authorizer): the guard's silent-refill check rejects any refill whose
         * signer is not the registered silent key. `None` on surfaces without a
         * hardware signer (test doubles).
         */silentKeyHex: String?, 
        /**
         * The EFFECTIVE silent capacity for the current period (smallest units):
         * `min(per-agent period-adjusted remaining, guard-global period-adjusted
         * remaining)`, NOT the per-agent remaining alone.
         *
         * Both caps bind on chain -- the guard's `refill` requires the amount to
         * be within each -- so reporting only the agent's remaining over-reports
         * (a 2 USDC agent allowance under a guard-global remaining of 0 can fund
         * nothing), and a caller that spends up to this number must find the
         * refill will allow it. Implementors of this trait MUST honour that: this
         * is the number the policy engine's Solana gates compare a spend against,
         * so a host that puts the agent remaining here alone makes the engine
         * approve silent spends the guard will reject.
         *
         * `None` until the agent is registered on-chain (no `Agent` account yet;
         * `add_agent` is a mobile-admin operation).
         */available: UInt64?, 
        /**
         * Per-agent per-period ceiling (smallest units). `None` until registered
         * on-chain.
         */ceiling: UInt64?, 
        /**
         * Reset period of the per-agent allowance (`day`/`week`/`month`/
         * `onetime`). `None` until registered on-chain.
         */period: Period?, 
        /**
         * Unix seconds of the allowance's last period reset. `None` until
         * registered on-chain.
         */lastReset: Int64?, 
        /**
         * Current pocket token balance (smallest units). `0` when the pocket ATA
         * does not exist yet.
         */balance: UInt64, 
        /**
         * Whether an on-chain `Agent` allowance account exists for this pocket.
         */registeredOnChain: Bool) {
        self.network = network
        self.mint = mint
        self.pocketAddress = pocketAddress
        self.agentPubkey = agentPubkey
        self.silentKeyHex = silentKeyHex
